      "prov": [],
      "orig": "For real-time determinations of I(j,k), the first row of the index array is permuted and the bytes corresponding to the permuted index are stored in the working memory. Then the next row is permuted and stored, etc. until all rows have been permuted and stored. The permutation of rows may be done sequentially or in parallel.",
      "text": "For real-time determinations of I(j,k), the first row of the index array is permuted and the bytes corresponding to the permuted index are stored in the working memory. Then the next row is permuted and stored, etc. until all rows have been permuted and stored. The permutation of rows may be done sequentially or in parallel."
    },
    {
      "self_ref": "#/texts/64",
      "parent": {
        "$ref": "#/texts/30"
